# Quake, Agent of S.H.I.E.L.D.: "Seismic Takedown - Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, tap target creature or land." Casting an
# Ornithopter (an artifact creature spell) triggers nothing (the stack holds the spell alone). Each Mox cast after it does: the
# first taps Bot2's Island (a land), the second Bot2's Ornithopter (a creature) - and Bot2's Mox Jet, an artifact that is neither,
# can't be chosen (the refusal). Bot2's own noncreature spell, a Mox cast on turn 2, triggers nothing for Bot1 ("you cast").

[Bot1 Deck]
Quake, Agent of S.H.I.E.L.D.
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mox Jet
Island
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Quake, Agent of S.H.I.E.L.D..Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = false
